core_changes:
Nothing is required outside mon.js/prologue.js: the route plays to the ending with only lines.js merged. Two optional, cosmetic changes, and one note:
1. vasco.js (cave 6, beamShown), so the mirror's spot walks onto the great triangle as Alan turns the seventh (the novel: it lands a metre right of the triangle, slides left onto its edge, then down to the centre). Replace
    if (ch() === 7) return f.lock_closed || f.disc_turned ? S.GREAT : S.DOOR;
with
    if (ch() === 7) {
      if (f.lock_closed || f.disc_turned) return S.GREAT;
      if (f.mirror_on) return [[S.GREAT[0] + 150, S.GREAT[1]], [S.GREAT[0] + 60, S.GREAT[1] - 10], [S.GREAT[0] + 20, S.GREAT[1] + 10]][Math.min(2, f.turn || 0)];
      return S.DOOR;
    }
   (f.turn is mon.js's count of correct turns, 0..3. The existing rule that hides the beam while f.cloud_over && !f.mirror_on stays as it is: the cloud now crosses at the seventh disc, not after the second.)
2. main.js PREVIEW.confession: the flags' placed list can follow the new order and the new flags: { ch: 7, lock_closed: true, placed: [1, 3, 2, 5, 4, 0], disc_turned: true, disc6_given: true, cloud_over: true, mirror_on: true, turn: 3 } (only membership of placed matters, so the current value still works).
3. The ending now passes through three of tue.js's rooms on Monday (hotel_lobby: Nieves's smile; canteras: Chano and San Borondón; hotel_room: the coffee), entered with { instant, noEnter, noSave } inside G.busy, so their enter hooks and autosaves never run; Alan stands alone in them (the narration carries Vasco; hotel_room hides the player for the morning). Optional, if the tue.js owner wants Vasco seen there: an npc in hotel_lobby and canteras with when: () => F().ch === 7 && !!F().won (no talk needed: nothing is clickable during the cutscene).

play_route:
  // ---- Monday
  await expect('Monday in Cave 6', () => Game.flags.ch === 7 && Game.room.id === 'cave6');
  await act('The door in the floor', 'use');
  // the novel's order: II, IV, III, VI, V, then Baute's disc in I
  await act('Socket I', null, 'discs'); // (wrong on purpose: the water surges)
  await expect('a surge', () => Game.flags.surges === 1);
  await act('Socket II', null, 'discs'); await act('Socket IV', null, 'discs'); await act('Socket III', null, 'discs');
  await act('Socket VI', null, 'discs'); await act('Socket V', null, 'discs');
  await expect('the sixth disc', () => Game.has('disc6'));
  await act('Socket I', null, 'disc6');
  // the seventh: the cloud crosses the sun; Carmen and the Land Rover's wing mirror; turned by the light as Vasco calls it
  await act('The seventh disc', 'use');
  await expect('the cloud', () => Game.flags.cloud_over && !Game.flags.mirror_on);
  await act('carmen', 'talk');
  await expect('the mirror', () => Game.flags.mirror_on);
  await act('The seventh disc', 'use', null, ['left', 'down', 'down']);
  await expect('the lock closed', () => Game.flags.lock_closed);
  await act('yeray', 'talk'); await act('vasco', 'talk', null, ['I have to tell you', 'I broke both']);
  await act('Path to the camp', 'exit'); await act('Camp radio', null, 'fuse');
  await page.waitForSelector('#ending:not(.hidden)', { timeout: 60000 });
  result = 'won';
} catch (e) { result = 'stopped: ' + e.message; }
console.log(JSON.stringify({ result, steps: step, errors: errs.slice(0, 20) }, null, 1));
await browser.close();
process.exit(result === 'won' && !errs.length ? 0 : 1);
